<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Learning About Our Diverse Cultures – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-style: italic;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Indigenous Heritage</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Learning About Our Diverse Cultures</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td colspan="3" style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write simple texts giving key information about oneself and one's culture. Interactive: Edit narrative texts written by peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a simple text sharing a personal cultural tradition (e.g., "Describe your family's celebration of Carnival and explain a key tradition, such as attending parades or dancing at the culcos."). Can edit a peer's narrative on Indigenous traditions by suggesting additional details (e.g., "I think you can add more details about the colors in traditional clothing."). Can edit a peer's descriptive paragraph on a festival (e.g., "You could add some adjectives like 'colorful' or 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid and fun.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task (Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This stage activates prior knowledge, introduces the lesson's focus, and provides initial language input through demonstration and clear explanations.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of images showing various Panamanian Indigenous groups (Guna, Emberá, Ngäbe-Buglé) and their traditional art, clothing, and customs (e.g., molas, woven baskets, dances). Students are asked to brainstorm and write down 3-5 words or short phrases in their notebooks that come to mind when they see the images, related to "cultures," "traditions," or "heritage." (e.g., <i>vibrant, colorful, patterns, beadwork, ceremony</i>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models writing a simple descriptive sentence about a cultural tradition, perhaps a family one. For example, the teacher writes on the board: "My family <b>celebrates</b> Christmas with a big dinner. We often eat traditional food and sing songs. This <b>custom</b> is very important to our <b>family roots</b>." The teacher highlights adjectives (e.g., "big," "traditional," "important") and verbs (e.g., "celebrates," "eat," "sing"). The teacher also models stress in multisyllabic words like "celebrates" and "important" while reading the sentence aloud.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What kind of information did I include about my tradition? (e.g., what we do, what it's like)"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which words helped make my description more interesting? (e.g., 'big,' 'traditional')"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">New language and content are presented in an authentic context, focusing on comprehension.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario "Our Indigenous Heritage":</b> The teacher presents a short descriptive paragraph about a specific Indigenous tradition from Panama, projected on the board. The text incorporates target grammar (present simple, past simple, adjectives, present perfect) and vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Example text:</i> "The Guna people, one of Panama's diverse <b>Indigenous</b> <b>cultures</b>, have a rich <b>heritage</b>. They are famous for their <b>colorful</b> 'molas,' intricate textile art with geometric <b>patterns</b>. For centuries, Guna women <b>have preserved</b> this <b>traditional</b> art form. The Gunas originally <b>migrated</b> to the San Blas islands in the 16th century, and they continue to <b>sustain</b> their unique <b>customs</b> and <b>language</b>. Their <b>vibrant</b> ceremonies often include traditional music and dances, celebrating their strong <b>community</b> and <b>identity</b>."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Descriptive paragraph about Guna Yala's traditional patterns and customs (genre: descriptive narrative, register: informative, format: text on screen/handout).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interpretive Competence – understanding and extracting key information from a written text to inform future writing tasks.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the text individually. Then, they answer a few short questions in writing:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the Guna people's famous art form?" (Gist question)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"True or False: The Guna people migrated to the islands recently." (T/F)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Find three adjectives that describe Guna art or ceremonies." (Information matching/scanning)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This stage focuses on controlled and semi-controlled practice of target language for accuracy, specifically in writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Accuracy focus on Writing.</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using present simple and past simple for descriptions, employing adjectives for detail, and the present perfect for ongoing actions. Focus on vocabulary: <i>Indigenous, cultures, traditions, patterns, diversity, heritage, preservation, customs, ancestry, vibrant, colorful, preserved, traditional, diverse, ancestral, cultural, historical.</i></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice – Sentence Completion (5 min):</b> Students complete sentences using target vocabulary and correct verb tenses based on the Presentation text or general knowledge about Indigenous cultures.</li>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: circle; margin-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The Guna people’s molas have really ______ (color/colorful) designs.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They ______ (preserve) their traditions for centuries. (Use present perfect)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The Emberá ______ (migrate) to different areas in the past. (Use past simple)</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Panama is known for its ______ (diversity) of Indigenous ______ (culture).</li>
                    </ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice – Descriptive Sentence Writing (7 min):</b> Students write two descriptive sentences each, using prompts provided by the teacher. Each sentence must include at least one adjective and one target vocabulary noun/verb.</li>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: circle; margin-left: 20px;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 1: Describe a piece of traditional Indigenous art. (e.g., "The Emberá's <b>beadwork</b> shows <b>intricate patterns</b>.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 2: Talk about how an Indigenous group sustains its customs. (e.g., "They <b>sustain</b> their <b>cultural background</b> through <b>ancient rituals</b>.")</li>
                    </ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Pre-writing – Idea Web (5 min):</b> In pairs, students create an idea web for a descriptive paragraph about a specific cultural tradition (either a personal one or one from an Indigenous group). They list key details, sensory adjectives (e.g., <i>vibrant, colorful</i>), and relevant verbs (e.g., <i>celebrate, preserve</i>). This helps them organize their thoughts for the production stage.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">17 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students use the language spontaneously in a realistic, communicative task, focusing on fluency and task completion.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Indigenous Heritage".</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task: "My Cultural Tradition or an Indigenous Custom" Descriptive Paragraph (Written Product).</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students choose one topic: (1) Write a simple descriptive paragraph (approx. 80-100 words) sharing a personal cultural tradition from their family or community (e.g., a unique celebration, a specific food tradition, a family custom). OR (2) Write a descriptive paragraph (approx. 80-100 words) about a specific custom, tradition, or art form from one of Panama's Indigenous groups, based on what they've learned in the unit. The paragraph must include at least 5 target vocabulary words (e.g., <i>heritage, traditions, colorful, patterns, preserve</i>) and use descriptive adjectives and appropriate verb tenses (present simple for general facts, past simple for historical details, present perfect for ongoing actions).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection:</b> Directly fulfills the objective of writing simple texts giving key information about oneself/one's culture or an Indigenous culture. Students engage in the pragmatic function of "Acknowledging cultural value" and "Sharing historical importance" through their writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in written expression, coherent organization of ideas, and effective use of target grammar and vocabulary to convey descriptive information. Students should feel confident using the stressed sounds of words like "Indigenous" and "ancestry" when silently formulating their thoughts.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This stage involves formative assessment and provides students with an opportunity for self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Peer Editing Checklist and Teacher Observation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their descriptive paragraphs with a peer. Using a provided "Peer Editing Checklist," students read their partner's paragraph and provide constructive feedback by ticking boxes and writing short suggestions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Peer Editing Checklist prompts:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is the main cultural tradition/custom clearly described? (Yes/No/Needs more detail)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are there at least 3-4 descriptive adjectives (e.g., <i>colorful, vibrant, traditional</i>)? (Yes/No/Suggest more)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are present simple and past simple used correctly? (Mostly/Sometimes/Needs practice)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can you suggest adding more details about colors, patterns, or history? (Write suggestion) (e.g., "You could add some adjectives like 'exciting' to make it sound more vivid.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Can you identify any target vocabulary words used? (List 1-2 words)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation during peer editing):</b> Accuracy in identifying areas for improvement in peers' texts, clarity of written feedback, constructive suggestions based on the learning outcome (e.g., suggesting more details or adjectives).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions in their notebooks:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one thing you did well in your descriptive paragraph?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one suggestion your peer gave you that you will use to improve your writing?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">This final stage encourages learners and the teacher to reflect on the lesson's effectiveness and plan for future learning.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt (done individually):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has learning to use more descriptive adjectives helped you to share information about different <b>cultures</b> today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new thing you learned about writing descriptions, especially when talking about <b>Indigenous traditions</b> or your own <b>cultural background</b>?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., peer editing, specific grammar practice, vocabulary integration)"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with descriptive writing or peer feedback? (e.g., more sentence starters, explicit modeling of feedback phrases)"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did students engage in 'Discuss the preservation of Indigenous cultures and propose ideas' implicitly through their writing?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> "Today we focused on writing detailed descriptions of cultural traditions and editing peers' work. In our next and final lesson, we will integrate these writing skills along with our listening, reading, and speaking practice to consolidate and summarize information for our 21st Century Skills Project, which will be a creative presentation or digital story about Panama's diverse Indigenous heritage."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>